# Line endings for generated output
#
# The build scripts in tools/ write their output with LF line endings.
# This clone has core.autocrlf=true, which tells git the working tree
# should hold CRLF. With no .gitattributes, git therefore treats every
# freshly generated page as "modified" even when the bytes are identical
# to the committed blob, and prints a "LF will be replaced by CRLF"
# warning for each one.
#
# That broke a check the audit runs depend on: every quality pass
# re-runs the six build scripts and treats a clean "git status" as proof
# that the committed pages still match what the generators produce. With
# 89 false positives in the way, real drift could not be told from noise.
#
# Declaring the generated directories as LF makes git stop trying to
# convert them, so the status check means something again. The rest of
# the repo is left alone: at the time of writing 47 files outside these
# directories hold CRLF and are untouched by this rule.
#
# Added 2026-08-06 during the quality pass on worklist item 3.1.

modules/service/pages/** text eol=lf
modules/switch/pages/**  text eol=lf
modules/branch/pages/**  text eol=lf
